{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"In **ResStock 2025 Release 1**:\n\n- **Heating setpoints range from 55°F to 80°F**, referring to base setpoints before any setback offsets.\n- **The distribution is built from U.S. EIA’s 2020 Residential Energy Consumption Survey (RECS) microdata.** Both details appear in §8.4.5, “Setpoints,” of the [2025.1 Technical Reference Guide](https://natlabrockies.github.io/ResStock.github.io/assets/trd/ResStockTechnicalReferenceGuide_2025_1.pdf).\n- **A 55°F setpoint indicates a vacant housing unit**, with heating maintained to prevent pipes from freezing. See §2, Figure 1’s footnote, on printed page 8 of [*ResStock Measure Documentation: HVAC Load Flexibility*](https://docs.nlr.gov/docs/fy26osti/93846.pdf#page=16)."}}
